<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-26--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-26: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.26";
    dc:description "The repair observation is an experimental report scored with the repair claims. The further statement that no current molecular or tissue model could have predicted it, and that this motivates a screen, is a judgment about the state of theory. No public analysis has a yes-or-no result that would confirm or refute unpredictability as stated.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Whether tracheal-derived cells were observed over neural tissue is a factual report. 'Could not be predicted from any current model' and 'unexpected given normal roles' do not specify a model class, a prediction threshold or an observation that would fail if some existing model had entailed the interaction.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A model written after the experiment, or a model that was never formalized, both fit the wording.", "Absence of a model from a database does not show that the outcome was unpredictable.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.66"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.262"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
